Subject: cthulhu: short-circuit cthulhu_cgroup_config on cgroup v2 hosts

cthulhu_cgroup_config() calls three sub-helpers in sequence:

  cthulhu_config_devices()       — writes devices.allow / devices.deny
  cthulhu_cgroup_config_cpu()    — writes cpu.cfs_quota_us / cpu.shares
  cthulhu_cgroup_config_memory() — writes memory.limit_in_bytes etc.

All three use v1-only cgroup file names.  cthulhu_cgroup_config_cpu has
an internal setting_exists guard so it returns 0 on a cgroup v2 host,
but config_devices and config_memory don't — they unconditionally
fopen("devices.allow", "w") etc. against a kernel-managed directory,
get EPERM / ENOENT, and propagate failure.

cthulhu_sb_start() then refuses to bring the sandbox to Up state.  EE
in the TR-181 view stays Disabled.  timingila rejects every InstallDU
with fault 7225 ("Deployment Unit to Execution Environment Mismatch",
which it also raises when EE.Status isn't Enabled).

This matters on any modern Linux host running cgroup v2 unified
hierarchy (most distros since ~2021).  cthulhu *does* detect the v2
layout (cgroup_layout_unified) but only branches on it for path
construction, not to suppress v1-only operations.

Pragmatic fix: when cgroup v2 is detected, return 0 from
cthulhu_cgroup_config() before any sub-helpers run.  The sandbox is
then "resource-unlimited" — acceptable for dev/test environments.
Real cgroup v2 limits would need v2-native setting calls
(cpu.weight, memory.max, device-cgroup BPF programs) — that's a much
larger porting effort and a candidate for upstream contribution to
gitlab.com/prpl-foundation/lcm/applications/cthulhu.

Tested in vcpe-002 LXC container running on a cgroup-v2 host:
sandbox transitions to Up, Device.SoftwareModules.ExecEnv.1.Status
becomes Enabled, obuspa's InstallDU completes end-to-end and a real
crun container appears in `crun list`.
---
 src/cthulhu_cgroup.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/cthulhu_cgroup.c b/src/cthulhu_cgroup.c
--- a/src/cthulhu_cgroup.c
+++ b/src/cthulhu_cgroup.c
@@ -651,6 +651,15 @@
  */
 int cthulhu_cgroup_config(const char* cgroup_name, amxd_object_t* sb_obj, cthulhu_notif_data_t* notif_data) {
     int res = -1;
+
+    /* vCPE: On cgroup v2 unified hosts the v1 setting file names
+     * (devices.allow, memory.limit_in_bytes, ...) don't exist; the v1
+     * config calls below would all return -1.  Short-circuit to success
+     * so the sandbox can transition to Up.  Resource limits are skipped. */
+    if(cthulhu_cgroup_layout_get() == cgroup_layout_unified) {
+        SAH_TRACEZ_INFO(ME, "cgroup v2 unified detected; skipping v1-style sandbox cgroup config for [%s]", cgroup_name);
+        return 0;
+    }
     if(cthulhu_config_devices(cgroup_name, sb_obj) < 0) {
         NOTIF_FAILED(notif_data, tr181_fault_request_denied, "Could not configure device cgroup for [%s]", cgroup_name);
         goto exit;
